    "reasons": [
      "The README shows clear indicators of deceptive intent (not just poor quality): installation/import examples and badges consistently reference \"string-master\" while the trusted package name is \"str-master\" — a classic typosquatting/impostor pattern intended to trick users into installing the wrong package. Additional red flags: placeholder links (your-username), unverifiable performance/test coverage claims, and copied template content. Although no executable malware is present in the README itself, the deliberate naming mismatch and impersonation indicate malicious/abusive intent."
    ]
